---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import ArticleSchema from "../../components/ArticleSchema.astro";
import InlineScheduler from "../../components/InlineScheduler.astro";
import LeadCapture from "../../components/LeadCapture.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Real Estate Mediation · Pro Se Fair Play Mediation"
  description="The marital home is often the largest asset in a Florida divorce. How real property is divided, what happens to the mortgage, and how mediation helps."
  ogImage="/og/guides.jpg"
>
  <ArticleSchema slug="real-estate-mediation" />
  <!-- ========================== HEADER ========================== -->
  <header class="article-header">
    <div class="container article-header-inner">
      <Breadcrumbs trail={[{ href: "/process", label: "The Mediation Process" }]} current="Real Estate Mediation" tone="light" />
      <p class="kicker reveal reveal-d1">
        <span class="kicker-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        Property &amp; Real Estate
      </p>
      <h1 class="display article-title reveal reveal-d2">
        Real Estate <span class="display-italic">Mediation</span><span class="display-italic">.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="lede reveal reveal-d3">
        The marital home is often the largest asset in a Florida divorce, and
        the hardest one to divide. Here is how real property is handled, what
        happens to the mortgage, and how mediation fits in.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- ========================== BODY ========================== -->
  <section class="article-body">
    <div class="container-narrow article-prose">
      <h2>The Marital Home in a Florida Divorce</h2>
      <p>
        For most families the house is the largest thing they own and the
        hardest thing to divide. A bank account can be split down the middle.
        A home cannot.
      </p>

      <h3>Is the Home Marital Property?</h3>
      <p>
        Equity built during the marriage is generally marital property, even if
        only one spouse is named on the deed. Florida courts start from the
        presumption that marital assets are divided equally. These rules come
        from Florida Statute §&nbsp;61.075.
      </p>

      <h3>The Three Common Outcomes</h3>
      <p>Most agreements land on one of three arrangements:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>The home is sold and the proceeds are divided.</li>
        <li>One spouse buys out the other's share and keeps the home.</li>
        <li>One spouse stays in the home for a set period, and the home is sold later.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>The Mortgage Is a Separate Problem</h3>
      <p>
        A divorce judgment divides property between the two of you. It does not
        remove anyone from the loan. Until the home is sold or the mortgage is
        refinanced, both spouses remain responsible to the lender, no matter who
        is living there.
      </p>

      <h2>What You Will Need to Decide</h2>
      <p>A workable agreement closes each of these questions:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>How the home is valued, and who performs the appraisal.</li>
        <li>Who pays the mortgage, taxes, insurance, and HOA dues until it sells.</li>
        <li>How repairs, upkeep, and closing costs are split.</li>
        <li>The buyout amount, and the deadline to complete it.</li>
        <li>What happens if a refinance is denied.</li>
        <li>Who keeps the furnishings.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        More complex situations, such as multiple properties, investment
        property, or the division of land, are handled through
        <a class="link-underline" href="/services/gold-service">Gold Service Mediation</a>,
        which brings a dedicated real estate professional into the process.
      </p>

      <h2>Real Estate Disputes Outside of Divorce</h2>
      <p>
        Not every property dispute comes out of a family case. These matters are
        handled as private mediation, chosen by both parties rather than ordered
        by a court. If a judge has already sent your case to mediation, ask the
        court which type of mediator it requires.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Co-owners or heirs who cannot agree on whether to sell.</li>
        <li>Buyers and sellers in disagreement after a closing.</li>
        <li>Landlords and tenants.</li>
        <li>Homeowners and contractors.</li>
        <li>Business partners who hold property together.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How Mediation Helps</h2>
      <p>
        A judge applies the statute and divides what is placed in front of them.
        In mediation you can build something a court order would not produce on
        its own: a sale timeline that works around the school year, a buyout paid
        in stages, or a refinance deadline with a fallback if the loan does not
        come through.
        <a class="link-underline" href="/process/how-mediation-works">How mediation works</a>
        walks through what a session looks like.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ========================== CLOSING CTA ========================== -->
  <section class="article-cta">
    <div class="container-narrow article-cta-inner">
      <a class="btn btn-primary article-cta-btn" href="/book">
        Book a Free, Private Consultation
        <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <p class="scheduling-note">Flexible Scheduling Available: Evening and Weekend Mediations to Accommodate Your Busy Life.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* Calendar inline, not a link to one — this is where the reader is
      already at peak intent. Lazy-loaded on scroll. */}
  <InlineScheduler source="guide-real-estate" />
  <LeadCapture source="guide-real-estate" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* ============================================================
     HEADER — cream, mirrors the legal pages
     ============================================================ */
  .article-header {
    position: relative;
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 6vw + 1rem, 6rem) clamp(2rem, 3vw, 3rem);
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse at 80% 20%, rgba(196, 154, 75, 0.08), transparent 55%),
      var(--color-cream);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-divider);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .article-header-inner { position: relative; max-width: 64rem; }
  .article-title {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: var(--step-5);
    line-height: 1.04;
    color: var(--color-navy);
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    max-width: 20ch;
    font-weight: 400;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .article-title .display-italic { color: var(--color-gold-deep); font-weight: 400; }
  .article-header .lede {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    max-width: 62ch;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }

  /* ============================================================
     BODY PROSE
     ============================================================ */
  .article-body {
    padding-block: var(--space-lg) var(--space-3xl);
    background: var(--color-cream);
  }
  .article-prose {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }
  .article-prose p { max-width: 64ch; }
  .article-prose p + p,
  .article-prose ul + p { margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  .article-prose h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--color-gold);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--color-navy);
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  .article-prose h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
    padding-top: 0;
    border-top: none;
  }
  .article-prose h3 {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 24;
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    line-height: 1.25;
    color: var(--color-navy);
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .article-prose ul {
    margin: 1rem 0 1.25rem;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    max-width: 64ch;
  }
  .article-prose li { line-height: 1.55; }
  .article-prose strong { color: var(--color-navy); font-weight: 600; }

  /* ============================================================
     CLOSING CTA — button only
     ============================================================ */
  .article-cta {
    position: relative;
    padding-block: var(--space-lg);
    background: var(--color-cream-warm);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-divider);
  }
  .article-cta::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0 0 auto 0;
    height: 1px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, var(--color-gold) 40%, var(--color-gold) 60%, transparent);
    opacity: 0.7;
  }
  .article-cta-inner { display: flex; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .article-cta-btn {
    background: var(--color-navy);
    color: var(--color-cream);
    border-color: var(--color-navy);
  }
  .article-cta-btn:hover {
    background: var(--color-navy-deep);
    color: var(--color-cream);
    border-color: var(--color-gold);
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .article-title { font-size: var(--step-4); }
  }
</style>
